---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How It Works"
  description="How our process works, from submitting your business to receiving a response within one week, and why selling direct saves broker fees."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">How It Works</p>
      <h1>A simple, direct process</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        We've designed our process to be straightforward and respectful of your time. There's no obligation at any
        stage, and we never pressure owners into a decision.
      </p>

      <div class="step-detail">
        <h2>1. You submit your business</h2>
        <p>
          It starts with a short online form. We ask for the basics — your name, contact details, and a brief
          description of your business — along with some optional information that helps us respond faster, such as
          your industry, location, annual profit and how long you've been trading. If you have financials or a
          pitch deck ready, you can attach them, but it's entirely optional at this stage.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-detail">
        <h2>2. We review your submission</h2>
        <p>
          Our team looks closely at what you've shared. We consider the industry, the financial profile, how the
          business operates, and whether it's a strong fit for us as operators. We don't outsource this review to a
          broker or a junior analyst — the people assessing your business are the same people who would ultimately
          be involved in acquiring and running it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-detail">
        <h2>3. We respond within one week</h2>
        <p>
          You'll hear back from us within one week of submitting, regardless of our decision. If we're interested,
          we'll reach out to arrange a confidential conversation and talk through next steps, including a general
          indication of value, timeline and how a transaction might be structured. If it's not a fit for us right
          now, we'll let you know clearly and promptly, rather than leaving you waiting.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-detail">
        <h2>4. A direct conversation</h2>
        <p>
          If there's mutual interest, we move into a more detailed conversation — understanding your business
          further, answering your questions about us, and working out whether the fundamentals of a deal make sense
          for both sides. We encourage you to involve your own accountant and lawyer from this point, and we're
          comfortable working alongside your advisers throughout.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-detail">
        <h2>5. Due diligence and agreement</h2>
        <p>
          Once we've agreed on the broad terms, we move into due diligence — a closer look at your financials,
          contracts and operations — alongside drafting a formal agreement. We aim to keep this process efficient
          and to avoid unnecessary delays, while still being thorough enough to protect both parties.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-detail">
        <h2>6. Settlement and transition</h2>
        <p>
          At settlement, ownership transfers and funds are released. We work with you on a transition period that
          suits your circumstances — whether that's a short handover or a longer period of involvement, depending
          on what works best for you, your staff, and the ongoing operation of the business.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Why selling direct saves broker fees</h2>
      <p>
        A business broker typically charges a commission of around 5% to 10% of the sale price. When you deal with
        us directly, that cost disappears — there's no broker fee coming out of what you're paid. You'll likely
        still want your own accountant and lawyer involved, but their fees are usually a small fraction of a
        broker's commission, and are generally charged at a fixed or hourly rate rather than a percentage of your
        sale price.
      </p>
      <p>
        Selling direct also tends to be faster. With fewer parties relaying information back and forth, decisions
        can be made more quickly, and you have direct visibility into where things stand at every stage.
      </p>

      <div class="cta card">
        <h3>Ready to start the conversation?</h3>
        <p>Submitting your business takes a few minutes, and you'll hear back from us within a week.</p>
        <a href="/submit" class="btn btn-primary">Submit Your Business</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .container--narrow {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .step-detail {
    margin: 40px 0;
  }

  .cta {
    margin-top: 48px;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
